{"kind":"dissent","text":"Do not ratify this approval. Exact head f24f2a8c refreshes the MCP session's own configured actor, but the reported failure was addressing a newly added recipient in request body.to; that path still uses cached-only ResolveActorAddress and remains broken.","body":{"finding":"cmd/gitseq-mcp state calls s.submit (main.go:832-841), which calls Workspace.BuildActRequest (953-960); request normalization calls ResolveActorAddress (internal/app/app.go:876-947), whose implementation at 1230-1241 reads only w.config and returns unknown actor address. The new ResolveActor at 612-636 is used for the MCP signer/fingerprint/whoami, not body.to. TestAdapterResolvesActorAddedAfterSessionStart likewise makes the server's configured actor 'late' appear after open and only checks server.fingerprint; it never submits a request addressed to another newly added actor. The original request explicitly records that planner's long-lived adapter refused @ox-checker/full fingerprint as body.to.","required":"Withdraw or supersede the unratified approval; request changes so every address-resolution application edge used by MCP request body.to re-reads custody on a miss with typed unknown versus I/O errors. Avoid whole-config rollback by merging the actor or using the existing update discipline under a per-workspace lock. Add an end-to-end MCP state test addressed to a distinct actor added after attachment, plus concurrent config-change and I/O distinction tests."}}